6,Exploring the Rich Soundscape of Congolese Music Heritage,https://shoutsmusic.blog/the-democratic-republic-of-the-congo-is-renowned-for-its-music/,"July 25, 2025 - French is the country’s official language, while Lingala, Swahili, Kituba, and Luba-Kasai have national status. From a musical perspective, Lingala remains the country’s dominant language. DR Congolese music originates from the traditions and customary practices of each ethnic group.",Swahili,Niger-Congo
7,Niger-Congo languages | African Language Family | Britannica,https://www.britannica.com/topic/Niger-Congo-languages,"July 26, 1999 - The Niger-Congo language family is the largest in Africa, spoken by approximately 85% of the population across a vast area. These languages have deeply influenced African culture and communication through music, oral traditions, and social structures.",Swahili,Niger-Congo
8,Soukous Music Genre History and Style Description| African Music Library,https://www.africanmusiclibrary.org/genre/Soukous,"In Kenya and Tanzania, soukous blended with local sounds like benga and taarab, forming a regional “Swahili sound.” A series of soukous albums produced by Virgin Records in the UK also sparked interest among world music audiences, contributing to the growth of soukous communities in Paris and other parts of Europe. In East Africa, soukous is known as ""Lingala"" music, referencing the language used in many soukous songs. In West Africa, it became known simply as “Congo music.” Soukous retained popularity in southern African nations like Zambia and Zimbabwe, where it is still sometimes referred to as Congolese rumba or rumba Lingala, highlighting its Afro-Cuban roots.",Swahili,Niger-Congo
